+## Model checks and the unfit sleep-environment boundary
+
+Most near-eye and complementary chest models were acceptable or acceptable
+with specified limitations. The four sleep-environment cells at each placement
+are **unfit for H05 inference** because their simulated residuals and fitted
+response support show material failures. Their estimates, confidence
+intervals, and p-values are suppressed. This judgment applies only to the H05
+response and model structure. It does not rule out analysing the underlying
+metric in another hypothesis with a different response variable, estimand, or
+model structure.
+
+A Tweedie model is a positive-response regression model that can accommodate
+right-skewed outcomes and exact zeros. For the sleep-environment outcome, that
+working model did not provide a defensible inferential representation.
+
